  "tech.abyssgeo.effect_desc": "Increases the Warmstone that accompanies Miner output by {effectPercent1}.",
  "tech.abyssgeo.name": "Abyssal Geology",
  "tech.abyssgeo.note": "Inspired by Civ VI’s Seafaring. Complete the Deep Mine upgrade; accompanying Warmstone output increases by {effectPercent1}.",
  "tech.adiabatic.name": "Thermal Insulation",
  "tech.adiabatic.unlock_desc": "The Europa Ice Launch Site can switch between Solar Sail mode and Dyson Node mode. Sail mode consumes per level per second: {sailUraniumRate} Uranium, {sailEngineRate} Strong Propellant Rocket Engines, {sailFilmRate} θ-Metal Adaptive Film, and {sailHydrothermalRate} Hydrothermal Energy. Node mode consumes {nodeUraniumRate} Uranium, {nodeEngineRate} engines, {nodeFilmRate} film, {titaniumPlateRate} Titanium Alloy Plates, and {nodeHydrothermalRate} Hydrothermal Energy per level per second. The Star Map opens the Dyson Sphere endgame panel; reach {solarSailGoal} Solar Sails and {dysonNodeGoal} Dyson Nodes to complete it.",
  "tech.alien_eng.name": "Large-Scale Alien Engineering",
  "tech.alien_eng.unlock_desc": "Unlocks the Mars Foundry. Construction costs {biomaterialCost} θ-Metal and {engineCost} Strong Propellant Rocket Engines. Each level produces Titanium and Titanium Plates.",
  "tech.ancient.effect_desc": "Reduces construction costs for all space buildings by {effectPercent1}. Multiple reductions stack multiplicatively, up to a total of {maximumReduction}. Stardust accumulates across runs and is awarded when a run is settled.",
  "tech.ancient.name": "Antediluvian Technology",
  "tech.apprentice.name": "Apprenticeship",
  "tech.apprentice.unlock_desc": "Unlocks the Fishbone Mine Sand Pit upgrade. Once purchased, it increases Miner Metal output by {effectPercent1} and accompanying Warmstone output by {effectPercent2}.",
  "tech.architect.name": "Megastructures",
  "tech.architect.unlock_desc": "Unlocks the Logistics Warehouse Workshop upgrade. The Caravanserai is renamed when upgraded; each level adds {capacityPerLevel} storage for capped materials unlocked through Era {eraCount}.",
  "tech.autodrill.unlock_desc": "Unlocks the Automated Drilling Workshop upgrade: Titanium and Uranium output increases with the share of active mines. Each active mine consumes {hydrothermalRate} Hydrothermal Energy/sec. Miners also begin collecting Uranium.",
  "tech.banking.name": "Banking",
  "tech.banking.note": "Inspired by Civ VI’s Banking: at Trade Zone level {zoneLevel}, the ledger becomes more valuable than the goods.",
  "tech.bigdata.name": "Big Data",
  "tech.bigdata.unlock_desc": "Unlocks Auto-Build for the Reef Core. The Auto-Upgrade toggle on the Buildings page applies to this zone.",
  "tech.biomat.name": "Biomaterials",
  "tech.biomat.unlock_desc": "Unlocks the Biomaterials Research Institute, which produces θ-Metal, and the θ-Metal Tool Set Workshop upgrade.",
  "tech.blackhistory.name": "Dark Blueprint",
  "tech.blackhistory.unlock_desc": "Crafting efficiency increases by {effectPercent1}, added to the Workshop crafting efficiency base.",
  "tech.blacksmoker.name": "Black Smoker Ironworking",
  "tech.blacksmoker.note": "Hot mineral slurry from black smokers is rich in iron sulfides. Enriching and refining it increases Iron output by a multiplier of {outputMultiplier}, stacking multiplicatively with Iron Working.",
  "tech.bronze.name": "Bronze Working",
  "tech.bronze.note": "Unlocks the Workshop, enabling the Coral-to-Bone Material and Metal-to-Iron processing lines.",
  "tech.calendar.effect_desc": "An information reward: reveals the Undersea Volcano’s cycle phase and readings. Does not affect resource output.",
  "tech.calendar.name": "Calendar",
  "tech.calendar.note": "Key Node.",
  "tech.canfill.effect_desc": "Each Hydrothermal Turbine level consumes an additional {metalPerSecond} Metal/sec and reduces its Pollution output by {effectPercent1}.",
  "tech.canfill.name": "Canned Landfill",
  "tech.canfill.note": "Seal exhaust in old cans and bury them under the seabed: Turbines consume an extra {metalPerSecond} Metal/sec per level, and this source of Pollution decreases by {effectPercent1}.",
  "tech.castle.unlock_desc": "Unlocks the Castle Council Hall upgrade. Once purchased, it reduces building costs; each level adds {capacityPerLevel} storage for capped resources unlocked through Era {eraCount} and produces {civicRate} Civic Points/sec.",
