  "ui.intro.achievements.description": "A collection of civilization milestones.",
  "ui.intro.achievements.title": "What is this? · Achievements",
  "ui.intro.challenges.description": "Optional, self-imposed rules for an entire run: no Insulation, a population cap, job limits, or a time limit. Harder challenges grant stronger permanent rewards.",
  "ui.intro.challenges.title": "What is this? · Challenges",
  "ui.intro.civic.description": "A Civic Tree that advances through the Eras. Civics unlock buildings, governments, and Policy Cards.",
  "ui.intro.civic.step": "Each government has different passive effects and a set number of Policy Card slots. Later governments have more slots.<br>Equip Policy Cards in slots to activate them.",
  "ui.intro.civic.title": "What is this? · Civics",
  "ui.intro.company.description": "Civilization's economic layer (unlocked by the Era {eraNumber} Civic Macroeconomics): the game automatically forms Kelp and Coral companies. They grow from local to regional to national over time, boosting the matching resource's production, while permanently increasing Luxury Goods consumption by {luxuryConsumptionIncreasePercent}.",
  "ui.intro.company.title": "What is this? · Companies",
  "ui.intro.faith.description": "The Faith system unlocks after researching Theology. Faith Points power religious bonuses.",
  "ui.intro.faith.step": "Faith left over from each Prestige accumulates as Old Faith, which benefits every subsequent Prestige.<br>Unlock Theology and establish a religion to earn Prestige Points when you Prestige.",
  "ui.intro.faith.title": "What is this? · Faith",
  "ui.intro.folk.description": "Population and jobs: Merfolk eat Kelp and need housing. Assign them to jobs such as Gatherer, Quarry Worker, or Scholar to drive production.",
  "ui.intro.folk.step": "When the population reaches its cap, build more housing. New people arrive only when Kelp exceeds {kelpThreshold}.",
  "ui.intro.folk.title": "What is this? · People",
  "ui.intro.meta.description": "Cross-run progression: a Shellbreak settlement grants Prestige Points, while reaching the Stars grants Stardust to spend on permanent bonuses in the shop.",
  "ui.intro.meta.step": "Unlock Theology to earn Prestige Points; Stardust is awarded after Shellbreak.",
  "ui.intro.meta.title": "What is this? · Prestige Shop",
  "ui.intro.star_dome.description": "Cross-run resource system: Stardust is awarded at Prestige settlement based on your space and alien facilities, Star Exploration progress, and Dyson Sphere progress. Spend it on permanent upgrades or exchange it for Prestige Points at a fixed rate.",
  "ui.intro.star_dome.step": "Building your first orbital satellite permanently unlocks this page. It stays open in future runs even if satellite levels reset. Stardust is credited on eligible Prestige settlements.",
  "ui.intro.star_dome.title": "What is this? · Stardust Shop",
  "ui.intro.star_map.description": "Unlocked after Shellbreak, the Star Map lets you explore your home star system early on and other star systems later.",
  "ui.intro.star_map.step": "The buildings here are the same as those in the Starfield Zone under the Habitat tab.",
  "ui.intro.star_map.title": "What is this? · Star Map",
  "ui.intro.tech.description": "A technology tree that advances through the Eras. Technologies unlock buildings, resource chains, and later systems.",
  "ui.intro.tech.step": "First, each technology is hidden until you meet its Eureka condition, which reveals its details and makes it available for research.<br>Next, researching an Era's key technology reveals the Eureka condition for the following Era, so you can prepare ahead.",
  "ui.intro.tech.title": "What is this? · Research",
  "ui.intro.village.description": "A list of every building you've unlocked in the Merfolk realm. Upgrade them here.",
  "ui.intro.village.step": "Manually gather Kelp and Coral until you have enough, then build a Deep-Sea Kelp Farm and a Reef Nest.",
  "ui.intro.village.title": "What is this? · Habitat",
  "ui.intro.wonder.description": "Major projects that cost enormous resources and grant powerful global bonuses or unlock endgame systems, such as the Sky Drill.",
  "ui.intro.wonder.title": "What is this? · Wonders",
  "ui.intro.workshop.description": "Process raw materials into advanced goods, and buy permanent crafting upgrades.",
  "ui.intro.workshop.step": "Higher crafting efficiency yields more advanced goods from the same materials.",
  "ui.intro.workshop.title": "What is this? · Workshop",
